# Installed to /etc/sudoers.d/pivpn-webui-agent on an AGENT box (with
# __USER__ substituted) — everything agent.py itself needs to run
# run_root()/_run_pivpn() calls relayed from the hub, and nothing else.
#
# Deliberately narrower than sudoers-pivpn-webui.template (the standalone/
# hub template): this box never runs the Flask app or the CD-deploy forced
# command, so it doesn't need the `systemctl restart pivpn-webui` or the
# `install ... /usr/local/sbin/...` grants that template also carries —
# both are specific to that other service existing on this box, which it
# doesn't on an agent-only install.
__USER__ ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/local/sbin/pivpn-webui-ccd-helper.sh
__USER__ ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/local/sbin/pivpn-webui-log-helper.sh
__USER__ ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/local/sbin/pivpn-webui-routes-helper.sh
__USER__ ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/local/sbin/pivpn-webui-client-script-helper.sh
__USER__ ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/sbin/iptables
__USER__ ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/sbin/iptables-save
__USER__ ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/sbin/netfilter-persistent
# persisted_rule_ids() reads the saved-rules snapshot back via this, as
# root, since the file is root:root 640 — see the standalone template's
# own comment on this exact line for the full reasoning.
__USER__ ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /bin/cat /etc/iptables/rules.v4
# pivpn itself internally runs each real subcommand as `sudo /opt/pivpn/...`
# — see the standalone template's own comment on this exact line for the
# full reasoning (same on an agent box as anywhere else this app runs).
__USER__ ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /opt/pivpn/*.sh, /opt/pivpn/openvpn/*.sh, /opt/pivpn/wireguard/*.sh
